# wear/woman/culturetunic_hang: the culture tunic's two-row skirt to mid-thigh: the hips, the split skirt, the lit hem band (the
# edge region); it parts at the side slits on the stride (wide), flares in the run, lies on the lap seated
# GARB-W (P2b wave 2). Fitted to one body (STYLE_P2 22). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# The side run (leg pass round 2, 2026-10-20): the side flare views (the run) kick the skirt up to the run hem, a row
# under the garment's lifted run views, so the legs show under it as limbs.
# The motion rebuild (2026-10-21, docs/MOTION_P2.md 7): the side walk takes torso=run (the belt row lifted with the hem),
# so the side `wide` views (contact, down) carry the torso rest's last row on top (no trouser band under the bodice) and
# reach a pixel further back over her fuller walking hip; the pass frames' rows are <garment>_stride.pxm's (keyed by the
# legs), so the rest and idle views (idles, hurts, falls, postures) are untouched. The run's flare is two rows (never a
# one-row spur behind the hips).
# WOMAN-WEAR (P2B rollout, 2026-10-22): the run `flare` trails the leaned torso (front level with the torso's hem front,
# each row lower a pixel further back, never reaching far behind: B10), covering whole leg rows (B11 HIPW, SLIVER); long
# skirts' walk `wide` hem rows swing a whole pixel forward on the contact and pass (rest on the reach): no glide.
use person woman
body woman
role garment culturetunic
layer hangFront
anchor hip
keys hang
sway 2

